 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests: tpm2-tools, pcscd
Description: TPM2-sealed TOTP codes shown before disk unlock
 tpm2-kira keeps a TOTP key inside the TPM and has the TPM compute the current
 code in the initramfs, before the root filesystem passphrase is requested. A
 code that appears proves the measured boot chain still matches the state the
 signing key approved; a missing code means something in that chain changed.
 The key never leaves the TPM, and code computation is locked when the real
 root takes over.
 .
 A legitimate firmware or bootloader update is approved with
 "tpm2-kira reseal" and the signing key, without re-enrolling the
 authenticator app.
 .
 On Debian the codes are shown from an initramfs-tools init-premount script, so
 no systemd in the initramfs is required.
